## From §5.2 (dihedral groups, 2026-09-24)

Nothing NEW is missing — §5.2 is blocked by the same finiteness gap as §5.1, and
the presentation half went through cleanly. Two notes worth keeping:

- **`rewrite` needs a TARGET STEP, not a bare formula.** Repeatedly I wrote
  `[by rewrite <equation> <something-that-was-not-a-step>]` and got "unknown
  reference". The fix each time was to introduce the target as its own step —
  often a trivial `[by reflexivity]` — and rewrite INTO that. Worth knowing
  before writing an equational chain.
- **`opAssoc` is stated `op(op(a,b),c) = op(a,op(b,c))`** — left-nested on the
  LEFT. Half my uses wanted the mirror and needed an explicit `[by symmetry …]`.
  Not a gap, just a direction to check before citing.

## Process notes worth keeping

- `bpa check tests/cases` (the whole fixture directory as one sweep) is a runaway
  — pathological fixtures, 6.8 GB RSS, >8 min. Use test_sweeps' curated dirs.
- Outside the repo, `zig` on PATH is asdf 0.15.2; scratch probes need
  `/home/ityonemo/.asdf/installs/zig/0.16.0/zig`.
- `tautology` is PROPOSITIONAL only — it treats a quantified statement as an
  opaque atom. A goal needing reasoning INSIDE a quantifier wants an explicit
  `fix` + `specialize`, not a tactic. Cost me two wrong turns in the parity work;
  the countermodel it prints is what makes this obvious.
- A test-harness failure message ECHOES the expected output. Twice I read those
  echoed lines as program output and went hunting for a nondeterminism bug that
  did not exist. Read what the gate ASSERTS before believing a diff.
